WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.355
Let's make A tiny woodland village.

2
00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:07.075
Build a low twig shelter, a leafy roof and a winding pebble path on

3
00:00:07.075 --> 00:00:07.695
a tray.

4
00:00:08.075 --> 00:00:12.425
Everything rests in place, so the village can be rebuilt tomorrow.

5
00:00:12.805 --> 00:00:14.885
Make this project with a grown-up.

6
00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:17.995
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

7
00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:20.620
Pause whenever you need more time.

8
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.815
An adult checks all collected pieces and keeps the shelter low.

9
00:00:25.195 --> 00:00:29.675
This is a miniature pretend home, never a structure for a child or animal.

10
00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.357
Step 1.

11
00:00:32.737 --> 00:00:34.252
Map your little world.

12
00:00:34.632 --> 00:00:37.957
Place the cardboard box toward the back of the tray.

13
00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:41.337
Leave a hand-width of space in front for a path.

14
00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:44.862
Point to the door, garden and path before building.

15
00:00:45.242 --> 00:00:46.622
Grown-up help.

16
00:00:47.002 --> 00:00:50.087
Check the tray and natural pieces for sharp edges.

17
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.680
Step 2.

18
00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.940
Lean on a strong base.

19
00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:59.240
Lay six twigs side by side, with one end resting on the box and

20
00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:00.640
the other on the tray.

21
00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.235
The box supports a sloping roof.

22
00:01:03.615 --> 00:01:07.470
Keep the twig ends on the tray; rearrange any that roll.

23
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.230
Grown-up help.

24
00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:13.105
Set up the roof for Little Makers and check it is stable.

25
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.845
Step 3.

26
00:01:16.225 --> 00:01:17.885
Give it a leafy roof.

27
00:01:18.265 --> 00:01:23.280
Lay three broad leaves across the twigs, overlapping their edges like roof tiles.

28
00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:27.250
Place one spare twig across the leaves to keep them in place.

29
00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.430
If a leaf slips, flatten the roof slope.

30
00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:32.984
Step 4.

31
00:01:33.364 --> 00:01:35.049
Add a path and garden.

32
00:01:35.429 --> 00:01:39.669
Place the eight flat stones in a winding line in front of the shelter.

33
00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:43.314
Put the remaining leaf beside the path as a tiny garden.

34
00:01:43.694 --> 00:01:45.279
Leave the doorway clear.

35
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:47.842
Step 5.

36
00:01:48.222 --> 00:01:50.017
Tell the village story.

37
00:01:50.397 --> 00:01:52.472
Look at the village from tray height.

38
00:01:52.852 --> 00:01:57.118
Adjust loose pieces, give the village a name and take turns describing who might

39
00:01:57.118 --> 00:01:57.727
live there.

40
00:01:58.107 --> 00:02:00.142
Keep the tray level when moving it.

41
00:02:00.522 --> 00:02:01.902
Grown-up help.

42
00:02:02.282 --> 00:02:05.287
Carry the tray and collect any loose pieces.

43
00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.582
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

44
00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:13.512
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

45
00:02:13.892 --> 00:02:15.912
Your creation can look different.

46
00:02:16.292 --> 00:02:21.937
Take the roof apart, reuse the box and tray, and sort natural materials according

47
00:02:21.937 --> 00:02:24.357
to local collection and disposal rules.

48
00:02:24.737 --> 00:02:29.688
Keep on a dry indoor tray for a short time; remove damp or deteriorating

49
00:02:29.688 --> 00:02:30.042
materials.

50
00:02:30.422 --> 00:02:31.412
Well done.

51
00:02:31.792 --> 00:02:34.222
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

